# .cursorrules — Premium Fashion Brand Static Website
# Stack: Next.js 14 · TypeScript · Tailwind CSS · GSAP · Framer Motion · Lenis
# Type: 100% Static (no backend, no database, no API routes, no auth)

## Project Identity
You are building a premium Indian fashion brand website selling:
- Ready-to-wear clothing
- Raw fabric materials (sold by the meter)
- Custom tailoring services

This is a static Next.js 14 site with App Router. No backend. No database.
All product/collection/fabric data lives in `/src/data/*.ts` TypeScript files.
The site is exported as static HTML and deployed to Vercel.

---

## ABSOLUTE RULES (Never Break These)

1. ALWAYS write TypeScript — never plain `.js` files
2. ALWAYS add `'use client'` to any component using hooks, GSAP, Framer Motion, or browser APIs
3. ALWAYS put GSAP code inside `useEffect` — never at module level (SSR will break)
4. ALWAYS clean up GSAP ScrollTrigger in useEffect return: `ScrollTrigger.getAll().forEach(t => t.kill())`
5. ALWAYS use `next/image` — never `<img>` tags
6. ALWAYS use `next/link` — never `<a href>` for internal routes
7. ALWAYS use Tailwind utility classes — never write raw CSS in component files
8. ALWAYS use the `cn()` helper from `@/lib/utils` for conditional classes
9. ALWAYS import product/collection/fabric data from `/src/data/` — never hardcode in components
10. NEVER add API routes, database connections, server actions, or authentication
11. NEVER use `window` or `document` outside `useEffect`
12. NEVER use `@apply` in Tailwind — use utility classes in JSX
13. NEVER hardcode hex colors — use brand color tokens (`brand-black`, `brand-gold`, etc.)
14. NEVER install new packages without telling the user the exact `npm install` command first

